WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.966
As our heroes keep travelling toward Anistar City,

2
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:10.133
they find time for a break at the local Pokémon Centre.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.933
- Man. That was so good.
- Yeah. It was yummy.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.066
Ne! Denne-denne!

5
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.400
Pika, pika!

6
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.566
Two more to go. Just two more Princess Keys. Mm-hm.

7
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.466
Cham, cham, cham.

8
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.666
I think we should try a new performance for the next Pokémon Showcase. Deal?

9
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:49.333
- Cham.
- Braix.

10
00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:55.600
Dumb twerpette. Who does she think she is?

11
00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:59.666
Doesn't she know I'm going to be the next Pokémon Showcase winner?

12
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:01.233
Probably not.

13
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.600
Now, for our next performance,

14
00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:08.466
I'm thinking we should modify the combination move we used last time.

15
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:09.600
- Braix.
- Cham.

16
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:14.600
Then let's review by going over the routine.

17
00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:16.900
Braixen!

18
00:01:16.966 --> 00:01:18.866
Pancham!

19
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:21.433
- Brai!
- Cham!

20
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.966
Great. That'll work. So, Stone Edge is up next.

21
00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.166
- Are you guys ready to go?
- Pan, cham-cham.

22
00:01:27.233 --> 00:01:29.766
- Braixen!
- Pancham-pan!

23
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:31.666
Braixen! -Cham, cham!

24
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:34.433
Pancham!

25
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.433
Brai, brai, brai, brai!

26
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.533
Brai!

27
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.800
Pancham! Pancham, pan!

28
00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.833
Braix!

29
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.500
- Braixen.
- Pancham. Pan.

30
00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:47.333
Braixen.

31
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.533
Brai!

32
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.933
Braixen!

33
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.866
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

34
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:02.633
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

35
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.066
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

36
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.533
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

37
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.366
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

38
00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:14.633
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

39
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.066
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

40
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:22.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

41
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

42
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

43
00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:36.666
Mending a Broken Spirit!

44
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.333
Brai...

45
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.700
Pancham, pan.

46
00:02:42.766 --> 00:02:44.366
- Brai! Braixen!
- Cham, Pancham.

47
00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:46.966
Wait. Come on, don't fight, you two.

48
00:02:48.466 --> 00:02:50.733
- Hey, what's the matter?
- Pikachu.

49
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.166
Braixen.

50
00:02:56.166 --> 00:02:59.966
- It broke when we were rehearsing.
- Pancham, Pancham.

51
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.200
- Oh, man.
- It's important to you, right?

52
00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:05.966
But it's not like Pancham did it on purpose.

53
00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.033
Braixen.

54
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:10.033
Cham.

55
00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:14.266
Cham... Cham!

56
00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:16.666
- Cham, cham, cham, cham...
- Where are you going?

57
00:03:18.466 --> 00:03:21.933
Cham, cham, cham, cham... Cham... cham...

58
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.400
Cham!

59
00:03:23.466 --> 00:03:25.400
Pan!

60
00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:27.833
Ch, ch, ch, ch! Cham.

61
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.100
Cham, cham, cham, cham, cham, cham, cham...

62
00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:32.866
- Look what Pancham found.
- Pancham.

63
00:03:32.933 --> 00:03:35.500
It's really nice you went to look for another branch.

64
00:03:35.566 --> 00:03:37.766
- Brai, Braixen.
- Braixen?

65
00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.033
Come on, Braixen, don't get so down.

66
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.700
All we have to do is go and look for a branch that it really likes.

67
00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:46.100
A branch that looks more like the original.

68
00:03:46.166 --> 00:03:50.100
- All right. Let's find it. Huh?
- Ne, ne, ne, ne! Denne-ne!

69
00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:52.433
It'll be fine. Don't worry.

70
00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.566
Brai. Braixen.

71
00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:04.333
Hm. I wonder what Braixen would like.

72
00:04:05.433 --> 00:04:07.366
Pan, Pancham.

73
00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:11.266
Pika.

74
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:15.066
- Hm. Hey, what about this one?
- Pika! Pi.

75
00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.633
Yeah, that one looks good too.

76
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.133
I sure hope we can find the perfect one.

77
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.966
- It'll be right if it's cute.
- Denne-ne!

78
00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:26.466
Huh. Aw.

79
00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:30.000
- Yay.
- Denne?

80
00:04:35.333 --> 00:04:37.000
Hm. Hm.

81
00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:40.566
Hm?

82
00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:42.833
Brai, brai, Braixen!

83
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.333
So you don't like any of them?

84
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.733
We tried to find branches that look like your old one.

85
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.633
- Guess we goofed.
- Denne-ne.

86
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.900
Brai!

87
00:04:54.966 --> 00:04:57.900
I'm sorry, Braixen. Everybody, just wait here.

88
00:04:57.966 --> 00:04:59.266
- Cham, cham.
- OK.

89
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.966
Hm. I'm worried.

90
00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.966
- Hey, let's go look again.
- Pika.

91
00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.900
- Uh. Right, let's go.
- Hm!

92
00:05:14.966 --> 00:05:17.733
Good idea. Yippee. Come on.

93
00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.833
- Insufferable.
- Why are you in such a snit?

94
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.366
Because of the twerps.

95
00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:32.833
Why can't those children try to understand how Braixen feels?

96
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.533
As far as Braixen is concerned, that branch is irreplaceable.

97
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.966
Really? Are you saying you understand Braixen's feelings?

98
00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.666
But of course. Be it person or Pokémon,

99
00:05:42.733 --> 00:05:44.966
the heart of a collector is one and the same.

100
00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:48.066
You must've experienced this too.

101
00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.600
Way back in the day, when we were, oh, so young...

102
00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:51.666
Huh?

103
00:05:53.066 --> 00:05:54.300
I'm home.

104
00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:06.066
I can't believe how rare this is. A beauty for my collection.

105
00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.100
Hm.

106
00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:16.266
Huh?

107
00:06:21.966 --> 00:06:24.433
My beautiful, irreplaceable bottle caps.

108
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.366
I threw those filthy things away.

109
00:06:29.733 --> 00:06:34.433
I had special memories associated with each and every one of those bottle caps.

110
00:06:36.066 --> 00:06:39.000
I'll never quite understand this whole collector thing.

111
00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:40.500
Tell me about it. Oy.

112
00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:45.633
Well, as a fellow collector, I can't turn a blind eye on this travesty.

113
00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.700
Yes! It's time to step up.

114
00:06:55.933 --> 00:06:58.466
- Oh, Braixen.
- Cham, cham.

115
00:06:58.533 --> 00:06:59.533
Braixen.

116
00:07:01.066 --> 00:07:03.566
But why does it have to be that specific branch?

117
00:07:03.633 --> 00:07:08.700
- Brai. Braixen!
- What do you mean?

118
00:07:08.766 --> 00:07:11.133
-Huh? Braixen! Wait!

119
00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.400
Oh!

120
00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.166
Huh?

121
00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.766
Mm. My name is Ja...

122
00:07:24.833 --> 00:07:25.900
Ahem.

123
00:07:25.966 --> 00:07:30.833
- I mean to say, my name is Jeeves.
- Jeeves? How do you do.

124
00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.433
My name is Serena. I'd like to introduce you to Pancham. And that's Braixen.

125
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.966
- Pan.
- Hm. What's that?

126
00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.900
I'm afraid Braixen's beloved branch broke.

127
00:07:41.966 --> 00:07:43.266
Braixen. Braixen.

128
00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:46.766
We're having a bit of trouble finding a replacement.

129
00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:50.166
Braixen must have a good reason to be so attached to it.

130
00:07:50.233 --> 00:07:52.266
Oh, I never thought about that.

131
00:07:52.966 --> 00:07:56.633
Hm. Huh? Now I remember.

132
00:07:58.366 --> 00:08:01.366
You did it! We can win this, Braixen.

133
00:08:01.433 --> 00:08:06.900
I'm going to become Kalos Queen, with your moves and that branch.

134
00:08:06.966 --> 00:08:08.300
Braixen.

135
00:08:08.366 --> 00:08:12.066
- Braixen? Do you mean...
- Brai.

136
00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.766
Is that why the other branches aren't right for you?

137
00:08:16.033 --> 00:08:17.566
Hm.

138
00:08:17.966 --> 00:08:20.666
Pancham. Pancham.

139
00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:25.100
Why don't we ask Nurse Joy at the Pokémon Centre if she can fix it for you?

140
00:08:25.166 --> 00:08:27.333
- Pancham, pan.
- Braix, Braixen.

141
00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.433
Good. She finally understands.

142
00:08:33.633 --> 00:08:35.766
We specialise in treating Pokémon.

143
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:39.133
I'm afraid repairing a broken branch is beyond my expertise.

144
00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.633
- I understand.
- Braixen, brai.

145
00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.400
I'm so sorry. I wish I could help you.

146
00:08:46.466 --> 00:08:50.133
Ah! I know. Please hold on one minute.

147
00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.966
I give up. So, what's James doin' dressed like that?

148
00:09:03.033 --> 00:09:05.966
He can't help sticking his nose into other people's business.

149
00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:07.833
It'll backfire, wait and see.

150
00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.033
Backfire? That's pretty harsh, even for you.

151
00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.533
Actually, I'd much prefer he'd catch both Braixen and Pancham

152
00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.800
for me instead.

153
00:09:15.866 --> 00:09:19.633
- What are you gonna do with them?
- Mess things up.

154
00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.900
If the twerpette can't enter the Showcase

155
00:09:21.966 --> 00:09:24.600
because she has no Pokémon, that's one less rival.

156
00:09:29.566 --> 00:09:33.200
Look at this. Mr Woodward's a famous tree surgeon,

157
00:09:33.266 --> 00:09:34.566
and he lives close by.

158
00:09:34.633 --> 00:09:40.300
He once reattached a Sawsbuck's horn, which everyone said would be impossible.

159
00:09:40.366 --> 00:09:42.833
- A tree surgeon?
- Brai.

160
00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.633
- Cham.
- That's right.

161
00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.933
He uses a method similar to grafting.

162
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.333
He filed down the branch to preserve the horn's exact dimensions,

163
00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.600
and then attached it perfectly.

164
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:55.500
If anyone can repair that branch, I'd say that he can.

165
00:09:55.566 --> 00:09:58.366
- You really think so?
- It's definitely worth a try.

166
00:09:58.433 --> 00:09:59.333
-Huh?

167
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.833
Brai!

168
00:10:09.466 --> 00:10:11.600
Gallade.

169
00:10:11.666 --> 00:10:13.233
Hm.

170
00:10:14.166 --> 00:10:15.700
Do you think you can fix it?

171
00:10:15.766 --> 00:10:17.166
- Pancham, cham.
- Braixen.

172
00:10:17.233 --> 00:10:19.200
Because you're a skilled wood specialist,

173
00:10:19.266 --> 00:10:22.466
repairing this branch should be quite easy for you, shouldn't it?

174
00:10:22.533 --> 00:10:23.633
Say you will, please?

175
00:10:25.333 --> 00:10:28.900
- It's not as easy as it appears.
- Gallade.

176
00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:34.233
But you were able to reattach that Sawsbuck's horn with skilled perfection.

177
00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.333
Yes, but that particular procedure was successful

178
00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.900
because the Sawsbuck had a powerful desire to reattach its horn.

179
00:10:40.966 --> 00:10:44.600
But we also have a powerful desire to get that branch repaired!

180
00:10:44.666 --> 00:10:45.666
Braixen, Braixen. Pancham.

181
00:10:47.333 --> 00:10:49.600
You'll have to show me that desire.

182
00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:53.433
That way, I'll be able to devote a hundred per cent to this procedure.

183
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.733
But how are they going to do that?

184
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.933
I think the best way is for you to consider

185
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.233
having your Braixen battle my Gallade.

186
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.866
The best way by far to get to know a Pokémon's heart

187
00:11:03.933 --> 00:11:07.000
- is during a Pokémon battle.
- Gallade!

188
00:11:10.366 --> 00:11:13.666
Yes, Serena went to see a tree surgeon just a little while ago.

189
00:11:13.733 --> 00:11:17.333
She went to a tree surgeon, huh? Wanna go, Pikachu?

190
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.000
Pika, pika!

191
00:11:19.066 --> 00:11:21.900
Who's that Pokémon?

192
00:11:26.066 --> 00:11:29.000
It's Gallade!

193
00:11:29.066 --> 00:11:30.900
Gallade!

194
00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.033
- Pi, pi...
- Huh?

195
00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.233
Huh?

196
00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:45.800
- There she is. Serena?
- Huh? It's Ash. You found me.

197
00:11:45.866 --> 00:11:50.833
- So, what happened with Braixen's branch?
- You see...

198
00:11:54.266 --> 00:11:57.233
- And that's what happened.
- Got it.

199
00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.300
So if you battle him, he'll fix Braixen's branch.

200
00:12:00.366 --> 00:12:03.900
Yeah. Show them how much you want that branch repaired.

201
00:12:03.966 --> 00:12:05.300
Pikachu!

202
00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:10.733
All right, then, if you don't mind, I'll be the referee.

203
00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:15.733
Trainers will each use one Pokémon. Is a single match OK?

204
00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.033
Hm.

205
00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:22.300
All right. Now, Braixen, let's show them just how strongly we feel about this.

206
00:12:22.366 --> 00:12:23.533
Braixen!

207
00:12:24.433 --> 00:12:27.500
Good. All right, then, battle begin!

208
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.766
Now then, I'm waiting for you to bring it on.

209
00:12:33.833 --> 00:12:37.766
Gallade! -All right! Braixen, use Scratch.

210
00:12:37.833 --> 00:12:41.800
Braixen!

211
00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:44.233
- Dodge it, Gallade.
- Gallade!

212
00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:47.000
- Brai!
- Gallade.

213
00:12:47.066 --> 00:12:50.500
I don't understand why they didn't use Flamethrower.

214
00:12:50.566 --> 00:12:54.166
Maybe it's difficult to use Fire-type moves because its branch is broken.

215
00:12:54.233 --> 00:12:55.233
Huh?

216
00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.466
Cham.

217
00:12:57.533 --> 00:12:59.166
Don't worry, Pancham.

218
00:12:59.233 --> 00:13:02.133
Braixen won't lose because of something like that.

219
00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.133
- You can do it, Serena.
- Pika!

220
00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.833
- Hm. Use Scratch.
- Braixen!

221
00:13:08.833 --> 00:13:10.233
- Brai!
- Dodge it, quick.

222
00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:13.233
- Braixen!
- Gallade!

223
00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.733
- Use Slash.
- Gallade!

224
00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.966
Braixen!

225
00:13:19.033 --> 00:13:20.500
Oh, no. Braixen got hit.

226
00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:23.700
They've already figured out the timing of Braixen's Scratch.

227
00:13:23.766 --> 00:13:26.166
- What are they gonna do?

228
00:13:26.233 --> 00:13:28.633
Guess Braixen needs that branch after all.

229
00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.400
Hm!

230
00:13:31.466 --> 00:13:34.400
They've all got their heads wrapped around that battle.

231
00:13:34.466 --> 00:13:36.866
The perfect time to grab Pikachu.

232
00:13:36.933 --> 00:13:40.966
Opportunity comes to those who wait. But Pikachu-catching time is now!

233
00:13:41.033 --> 00:13:43.866
- All right, and how!
- You can still battle.

234
00:13:43.933 --> 00:13:46.300
- Right, Braixen?
- Braixen.

235
00:13:46.366 --> 00:13:47.633
Use Psycho Cut.

236
00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.300
Gallade!

237
00:13:49.366 --> 00:13:51.966
Quickly, Braixen, dodge it.

238
00:13:55.566 --> 00:13:57.400
Pikachu!

239
00:13:59.133 --> 00:14:00.133
Pika!

240
00:14:01.733 --> 00:14:04.366
Uh, could that be Jessie and Meowth's doing?

241
00:14:04.433 --> 00:14:06.066
Hey, what just happened?

242
00:14:06.133 --> 00:14:08.466
Prepare for trouble, you really don't know?

243
00:14:10.433 --> 00:14:13.366
Get over it, James. Enough of your show!

244
00:14:13.433 --> 00:14:15.100
Oh well, duty calls.

245
00:14:15.166 --> 00:14:17.733
- Mm!
- Aah!

246
00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:21.333
- And twirl!
- And stick!

247
00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.000
Prepare for trouble, let's try this again!

248
00:14:24.066 --> 00:14:26.333
And make it double, we're clever times ten!

249
00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.833
To protect the world from devastation!

250
00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.766
To unite all people within our nation!

251
00:14:31.833 --> 00:14:34.700
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

252
00:14:34.766 --> 00:14:38.066
To extend our reach to the stars above!

253
00:14:38.133 --> 00:14:40.300
- Jessie!
- And James.

254
00:14:40.366 --> 00:14:43.133
Team Rocket regroups at the speed of light!

255
00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.366
Surrender now. A future with Pikachu looks bright!

256
00:14:46.433 --> 00:14:47.866
Meowth, that's right!

257
00:14:47.933 --> 00:14:48.933
Wobbuffet!

258
00:14:51.133 --> 00:14:52.500
It's Team Rocket.

259
00:14:52.566 --> 00:14:55.066
- What in the world were you thinking?
- Not much.

260
00:14:55.133 --> 00:14:58.466
- Wait a minute. Do you know them?
- Too well.

261
00:14:58.533 --> 00:15:01.700
- They like to steal people's Pokémon.
- They do?

262
00:15:01.766 --> 00:15:04.133
Pay attention and give me that gizmo, now.

263
00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.933
- Oh, my!
- Aah!

264
00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.500
-This time, I'll aim it correctly.

265
00:15:10.566 --> 00:15:13.133
I don't have time to deal with this nonsense.

266
00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.500
- Hey, Ash? Give me a hand.
- Sure.

267
00:15:15.566 --> 00:15:18.300
OK, Braixen and Pancham, are you ready?

268
00:15:18.366 --> 00:15:19.500
- Cham.
- Braixen.

269
00:15:19.566 --> 00:15:23.000
Pancham!

270
00:15:23.066 --> 00:15:26.500
Braixen! Xen!

271
00:15:27.533 --> 00:15:30.000
Braixen!

272
00:15:36.233 --> 00:15:38.400
- Did you just see that move?
- I did.

273
00:15:38.466 --> 00:15:42.500
It might have been a coincidence, but it sure looked just like a Fire Blast.

274
00:15:42.566 --> 00:15:44.700
Pikachu, use Thunderbolt now.

275
00:15:44.766 --> 00:15:45.866
Pikachu!

276
00:15:47.333 --> 00:15:48.333
This is getting old.

277
00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.833
Pikachu!

278
00:15:54.566 --> 00:15:56.700
Great new move, Braixen.

279
00:15:56.766 --> 00:15:58.233
Braixen's quite eager.

280
00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.600
So won't you please fix Braixen's branch, Woodward?

281
00:16:01.666 --> 00:16:03.500
Why would you care about a dumb branch?

282
00:16:03.566 --> 00:16:06.766
Why not? I'm feeling great today.

283
00:16:06.833 --> 00:16:09.033
I guess bein' a chump will do that to you.

284
00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:12.033
- We're blasting off again!
- Wobbuffet!

285
00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:19.833
Woodward, please. Let our battle continue.

286
00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:23.866
- And please agree to fix Braixen's branch.
- My dear child.

287
00:16:23.933 --> 00:16:26.633
I'm afraid that branch was already well beyond repair

288
00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:29.733
from the very first time you brought it to my attention.

289
00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.466
- But...
- Now, Braixen...

290
00:16:31.533 --> 00:16:34.433
You know why we did all this, don't you?

291
00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.800
Why I asked you to have a battle with me?

292
00:16:37.866 --> 00:16:39.533
You see, there's nothing wrong

293
00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.466
with wanting to hold onto precious things from the past.

294
00:16:42.533 --> 00:16:46.966
But becoming overly attached can keep you stuck in the past as well.

295
00:16:48.766 --> 00:16:50.466
Brai...

296
00:16:50.533 --> 00:16:55.333
You tried Flamethrower with your broken branch and it ended up as a Fire Blast.

297
00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.500
It was unintentional, but you could use the move with that branch

298
00:16:58.566 --> 00:17:00.766
because your feeling was so strong.

299
00:17:00.833 --> 00:17:04.733
And if you are able to hold onto that strong desire of yours,

300
00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:09.333
I'm sure you'll be able to master anything you possess.

301
00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:11.266
Braxien.

302
00:17:11.333 --> 00:17:14.666
Pancham, pan. Pancham, cham, cham, cham.

303
00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:16.266
- Cham!
- Huh?

304
00:17:16.333 --> 00:17:18.333
Pancham.

305
00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.866
Oh, Pancham.

306
00:17:24.933 --> 00:17:27.300
Cham, cham.

307
00:17:27.366 --> 00:17:28.500
Hey, you know what?

308
00:17:29.433 --> 00:17:32.500
I didn't become Kalos Queen with the branch you had

309
00:17:32.566 --> 00:17:34.433
when we made our promise together,

310
00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:40.000
so let's make a new promise with the branch Pancham wants to give you.

311
00:17:40.966 --> 00:17:45.533
It's time for us to write the next chapter of our partnership.

312
00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:54.066
- Brai!
- It's all for one. Let's do this together.

313
00:17:54.133 --> 00:17:57.066
- Pancham, cham.
- Braixen.

314
00:18:00.933 --> 00:18:04.366
This is to remember the promise we've made.

315
00:18:06.466 --> 00:18:09.333
Brai! Braixen!

316
00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.333
- All right. Let's try it out.
- Braixen!

317
00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.433
Now, let's get back to our battle.

318
00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.666
All right, then. Let the battle resume.

319
00:18:18.733 --> 00:18:21.100
OK, Gallade, use Psycho Cut.

320
00:18:21.166 --> 00:18:22.466
Gallade!

321
00:18:22.533 --> 00:18:25.466
- Quick, Braixen, dodge it.
- Braixen!

322
00:18:25.533 --> 00:18:28.066
- Use Fire Blast.
- Braix!

323
00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.333
Gallade!

324
00:18:33.533 --> 00:18:35.200
Brai!

325
00:18:36.333 --> 00:18:38.900
Gallade...

326
00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.800
That will be all, now. Excellent work.

327
00:18:42.866 --> 00:18:44.500
- Gallade, you were great.
- Ga.

328
00:18:44.566 --> 00:18:47.000
- Braixen!
- Braixen!

329
00:18:47.066 --> 00:18:48.733
- We won!
- Pancham.

330
00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.733
- Pancham!
- Brai! Braixen!

331
00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:54.100
I'm really so happy Braixen's feeling better again.

332
00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:55.166
- Yeah.
- Braixen!

333
00:18:55.233 --> 00:18:57.500
That Fire Blast really showed us how Braixen felt.

334
00:18:57.566 --> 00:19:00.200
- Yippee, yay!
- Denne!

335
00:19:00.266 --> 00:19:02.466
All right, my friend.

336
00:19:02.533 --> 00:19:05.433
I think it's about time we both got back to work.

337
00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.000
Ga, Gallade.

338
00:19:07.066 --> 00:19:09.500
What are you gonna do with those?

339
00:19:09.566 --> 00:19:12.166
I thought you said that branch wasn't fixable.

340
00:19:12.233 --> 00:19:14.433
Yes, I did say that.

341
00:19:15.966 --> 00:19:19.166
- However...
- Huh?

342
00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:26.400
Just as it should be.

343
00:19:31.833 --> 00:19:36.400
That branch will now begin a brand-new life right here.

344
00:19:37.366 --> 00:19:40.500
There will come a day when it will be useful to someone again.

345
00:19:40.566 --> 00:19:42.966
- Gallade.
- Braixen.

346
00:19:43.033 --> 00:19:47.833
And someday, we'll come back here and tell it all about our big success.

347
00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:49.333
Pancham.

348
00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:54.333
Remember, the promise we made with you is still with us.

349
00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:04.133
We've learned so much from you, Woodward.

350
00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.900
I can't thank you enough for your generosity.

351
00:20:06.966 --> 00:20:10.400
Now, now. I haven't really done much of anything at all.

352
00:20:10.466 --> 00:20:14.400
It's something you and your Pokémon learned together, my dear child.

353
00:20:14.466 --> 00:20:16.966
- I wanna thank you anyway.
- Pika, pika!

354
00:20:17.033 --> 00:20:21.300
- I also want to.
- We'll be back to visit for sure.

355
00:20:21.366 --> 00:20:23.466
Anybody have an idea where Jeeves went?

356
00:20:23.533 --> 00:20:24.633
-Pika?

357
00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:29.000
- You mean the guy with the glasses?
- He just disappeared, didn't he?

358
00:20:29.066 --> 00:20:33.000
- It's like he vanished into thin air. Huh?
- Pika.

359
00:20:33.066 --> 00:20:36.933
Braixen's broken branch and the promise that went with it

360
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.866
have given rise to a new promise, and a new branch.

361
00:20:39.933 --> 00:20:44.666
Now, Serena, Pancham, and Braixen look forward to winning the Pokémon Showcase

362
00:20:44.733 --> 00:20:49.733
with renewed confidence, as the journey continues.
